# Shared work tree ignore rules.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A BLANKET RULE. Two git repositories share this work tree:
#   .git     distributable build artifacts (minified_apks/) -- see .git/info/exclude
#   .gitsrc  the source revision history   -- driven by ./src-history.sh
# A rule here applies to BOTH, and to every tool that honors .gitignore. This file used to be a
# bare '*', which hid untracked source from `git status` in .gitsrc (so new files were never
# offered for commit and several went missing for days) and made ripgrep return no matches for
# anything in the tree. Keep the rules here specific.

# Build output
build/
.gradle/
.cxx/
.kotlin/
captures/
*.hprof

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
local.properties

# Signing material and secrets -- never commit these
*.jks
*.keystore
*.pk8
*.pem
*.p12
keystore.properties
arco.properties

# Distributables (the artifact repo un-ignores minified_apks/ in its own exclude file)
*.apk
*.aab

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Folded in from .gitsrc-ignore, which was never wired to anything. Git does not read a file by
# that name: those rules needed to be core.excludesFile or .gitsrc/info/exclude, so every one of
# them had been inert since it was written. They work from here.
.gitsrc/
*.log
.DS_Store

# 30 MB of packed projectM presets, built from app/src/main/assets/hione_presets. Not tracked in
# any of the three repos; listed so it stops reading as an untracked file someone should add.
app/src/main/assets/presets_pack.zip

# One-off patch scripts with hardcoded absolute paths, already applied. Not history material.
/check_img.py
/fix_manifest.py
/patch_gestures.py
